  "style": {
    "es": "Address the user as 'tú' (informal, the current software convention). Menu items and buttons: infinitive ('Abrir archivo'). Sentence case: only the first word and proper names capitalized.",
    "pt-BR": "Brazilian Portuguese. Address the user as 'você'. Menu items and buttons: infinitive ('Abrir arquivo'). Sentence case. Never use European-only words (see variantOnly.pt-PT).",
    "pt-PT": "European Portuguese, Acordo Ortográfico 1990 spelling. Avoid pronouns; use impersonal phrasing or the infinitive ('Abrir ficheiro'). Gerunds become 'a' + infinitive ('a carregar'). Sentence case. Never use Brazilian-only words (see variantOnly.pt-BR).",
    "de": "Address the user as 'Sie'. Menu items and buttons: infinitive at the end ('Datei öffnen'). Capitalize nouns as German requires; no English title case. Prefer short compounds; respect maxChars with a shorter synonym, not an abbreviation nobody uses.",
    "hu": "Impersonal UI style: avoid 'Ön' and 'te' where possible. Menu items and buttons: nominal forms ('Megnyitás', 'Mentés') or short infinitives. Sentence case. Never attach a suffix to a placeholder: phrase around it ('A(z) {name} fájl törlése?')."
  },
